# f(q)=1+∑ₙ₌₁∞q⁽ⁿ²⁾÷∏ⱼ₌₁ⁿ(1+qʲ)²

\[f(q)=1+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{q^{n^2}}{\prod_{j=1}^{n}(1+q^j)^2}\]

Ramanujan's third-order mock theta function f(q), distinct from a generic Hecke newform named f. Dunn introduces this in the discussion of partition ranks and half-integral-weight Maass methods.

## Where this expression comes from

- **Alexander Dunn (2020) — Analytic and Arithmetic Applications of Half Integral Weight Automorphic Forms**: [source notes](../books/theses/dunn/README.md); Chapter 1, §1.2, equation (1.2), printed p. 2 (PDF p. 9). [Document or source](https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/items/115703/bitstreams/378457/data.pdf#page=9). Ramanujan's third-order mock theta q-series; not a holomorphic newform L-series. **Evidence:** verified in source PDF or existing notes.

## Filename

The UTF-8 Git filename is the expression above (without a Markdown extension). The glyph **÷** in filenames denotes division, not ring quotient. Mathematical notation and hypotheses are stated in the displayed formula and provenance rather than relying solely on the filename.
